    "title": "Shell trap set to run a command",
    "desc": "A shell trap was armed to run a command on a signal or on exit - `trap \"<cmd>\" EXIT`, SIGINT, DEBUG, ERR. A trap re-runs its command every time the shell catches that event, so it is a tidy persistence/triggered-execution foothold (MITRE T1546.005) that survives inside any shell the attacker gets. A bare `trap` that only lists or clears handlers is not matched; a trap that binds a command to a signal is.",
